<%#
  The quote request list, with two additions to Administrate's default index: the current notification state,
  and a link to the screen that changes it.

  WHY IT IS HERE AND NOT ONLY IN THE DOCS. MARKETING_QUOTE_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL has no fallback of any kind
  (custom/app/mailers/marketing/quote_notification.rb), so while it is unset the mailer sends nothing at all
  and this page is the ONLY place a lead arrives. An operator who believes they are emailed about new
  requests, and is not, stops checking this page -- which is the failure the banner prevents. It is the same
  statement, for the same reason, as the one on the Platform Support desk
  (app/views/super_admin/platform_support/show.html.erb:27-38).

  THE STATE COMES FROM Marketing::QuoteSettings.status, the same method the settings screen renders, so the
  two pages cannot disagree about whether notifications are working.

  The rest of the file is Administrate's own index template, unchanged, so the search bar, table and
  pagination keep working as the gem updates them.
%>
<%=
  render("index_header",
    resources: resources,
    search_term: search_term,
    page: page,
    show_search_bar: show_search_bar)
%>

<section class="main-content__body main-content__body--flush">
  <% case Marketing::QuoteSettings.status %>
  <% when :unconfigured %>
    <div class="border border-yellow-300 bg-yellow-50 rounded-md px-3 py-2 mb-5 text-sm text-yellow-900">
      <strong>No quote notification address is configured</strong>, so nobody is emailed when a visitor
      submits the form on the pricing page. Every submission is still saved and listed here &mdash; this page
      is the only place they arrive.
      <%= link_to 'Set the address in Website Sales Settings', super_admin_marketing_settings_path,
                  class: 'underline font-semibold' %>.
    </div>
  <% when :failing %>
    <div class="border border-red-300 bg-red-50 rounded-md px-3 py-2 mb-5 text-sm text-red-900">
      <strong>The last quote notification could not be delivered</strong>, so the lead below may not have
      reached anybody by email. The requests themselves are safe.
      <%= link_to 'See what the mail server said', super_admin_marketing_settings_path,
                  class: 'underline font-semibold' %>.
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# The settings link is here whatever the state. The owner's brief asks for the address to be reachable
      from this screen rather than from an undocumented configuration key, and a link that appears only when
      something is wrong is not where an operator looks to CHANGE a working address. %>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-5">
    Quote requests are emailed to
    <% if Marketing::QuoteSettings.configured? %>
      <code><%= Marketing::QuoteSettings.address %></code>.
    <% else %>
      nobody yet.
    <% end %>
    <%= link_to 'Website Sales Settings', super_admin_marketing_settings_path,
                class: 'text-woot-600 underline' %>
  </p>

  <%= render(
    "collection",
    collection_presenter: page,
    collection_field_name: resource_name,
    page: page,
    resources: resources,
    table_title: "page-title") %>

  <%= render("pagination", resources: resources) %>
</section>
